.TH CFX 1 "July 26, 2026" "cfx" "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
cfx \- the small, auditable, two-command Codeforces workflow
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cfx
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR directory ]
.I problem
.br
.B cfx
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR directory ]
.B submit
.RB [ \-\-manual ]
.RB [ \-\-rebuild ]
.RB [ \-\-remote-check ]
.RI [ problem ]
.br
.B cfx
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR directory ]
.B test
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ problem ]
.br
.B cfx
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR directory ]
.B stress
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ problem ]
.br
.B cfx
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR directory ]
.B fail
.RI [ problem ]
.br
.B cfx
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR directory ]
.B bundle
.RB [ \-o
.IR file ]
.RI [ problem ]
.br
.B cfx
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR directory ]
.B get
.IR problem | contest
.br
.B cfx
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR directory ]
.B cc
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B cfx help
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cfx
manages an ordinary C++20 Codeforces solution archive.
The in-contest workflow is:
.PP
.nf
cfx 71A
cfx submit
.fi
.PP
The first command imports the problem, samples, and limits; creates its archive
directory; and opens
.IR solution.cpp .
The second tests and checked-compiles the exact bundled source, submits it
with the contest form in the signed-in browser, and waits for the Codeforces
verdict.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.I problem
Fetch a Codeforces problem through the browser connector, import its samples
and limits, create its archive directory, open
.IR solution.cpp ,
and remember it as the current problem. Official contest mirrors are tried when
Codeforces does not serve the statement.
.TP
.BI "get " problem
Create one problem directory without opening the editor.
.TP
.BI "get " contest
Create directories for every problem in a numeric contest.
Problem indexes are obtained from the official Codeforces API.
.TP
.BR test " [" problem "]"
Bundle and compile the solution, then run fetched samples followed by
handwritten cases.
Report OK, WA, RE, TLE, MLE, or OLE together with CPU time, wall time, and
peak memory.
With
.BR \-\-remote-check ,
report an output preview as unchecked instead of comparing it with the saved
answer. This does not establish correctness.
Builds are cached by source, compiler version, and compiler flags.
.TP
.BR stress " [" problem "]"
Compile the solution, generator, and brute-force implementation.
Generate deterministic inputs and compare the solution output with the
brute-force output.
The default files are
.I stress/gen.cpp
and
.IR stress/brute.cpp .
The generator receives the current seed as its final argument.
On a mismatch, the input, expected output, actual output, and seed are recorded
in external cfx state.
.B cfx
does not write the generator or brute-force source.
.TP
.BR fail " [" problem "]"
Promote the latest recorded stress mismatch to
.I cases/stress-N.in
and
.IR cases/stress-N.out .
The mismatch then becomes a permanent regression test.
.TP
.BR bundle " [" problem "]"
Recursively expand project-local quoted includes into a single
submission-ready source file.
System includes are preserved, and repeated local headers are included once.
.TP
.B cc
Listen for Competitive Companion JSON and import its samples.
Fetched samples remain separate from handwritten cases.
.TP
.BR submit " [" problem "]"
Run every saved test, build the submission profile, checked-compile the exact
bundled source, and submit it through Chrome.
With
.BR \-\-remote-check ,
execution failures still stop submission, but Codeforces validates the output.
Wait for judging and report the verdict, tests passed, execution time, and
memory consumption.
Only an
.B OK
verdict on
.B TESTS
is reported as Accepted.
A
.B PRETESTS
verdict or known pending submission exits 2; a final non-Accepted verdict
exits 1.
No Codeforces password or session cookie is read or stored by
.BR cfx ,
which never pushes.
.TP
.BR help " [" command "]"
Display general help or help for one command.
.SH TEST OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-checked
Compile with stricter warnings, AddressSanitizer, and
UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer.
.TP
.B \-\-rebuild
Ignore an existing cached binary.
.TP
.B \-\-remote-check
For
.B test
and
.BR submit ,
run saved inputs under their limits without comparing output to the saved
answers. Print an output preview and leave correctness to Codeforces.
.TP
.BI "\-\-time-limit " seconds
Override the fetched time limit.
.TP
.BI "\-\-memory-limit " MiB
Override the fetched memory limit.
.TP
.BI "\-\-output-limit " MiB
Override the output limit.
The default is 64 MiB.
.SH STRESS OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-gen " file
Use an alternative generator.
.TP
.BI "\-\-brute " file
Use an alternative brute-force implementation.
.TP
.BR \-n " " count ", " \-\-count " " count
Run
.I count
generated tests.
The default is 100.
.TP
.BI "\-\-seed " number
Set the initial seed.
The default is 1.
.TP
.BI "\-\-gen-arg " argument
Pass an additional argument to the generator.
This option may be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-checked
Checked-compile the solution and brute-force implementation.
.TP
.B \-\-rebuild
Ignore cached binaries.
.TP
.BI "\-\-time-limit " seconds
Set the solution and brute-force timeout.
.TP
.BI "\-\-generator-time-limit " seconds
Set the generator timeout.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Print the result of every seed.
.SH OTHER OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o " " file ", " \-\-output " " file
Write bundled source to
.I file
instead of standard output.
.TP
.B \-\-manual
Copy the tested bundle to the clipboard and open the Codeforces submission
page instead of using the connector.
.TP
.BI "\-\-host " address
Set the Competitive Companion listening address.
The default is 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.BI "\-\-port " port
Set the Competitive Companion port.
The default is 27121.
.TP
.B \-\-once
Import one Competitive Companion package and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Replace existing fetched samples when their contents differ.
.TP
.BI "\-\-root " directory
Use
.I directory
as the solution archive root.
.SH PROBLEM IDENTIFIERS
Problems may be specified as:
.PP
.nf
71A
A.71
A 71
https://codeforces.com/contest/71/problem/A
codeforces/71/A
.fi
.PP
When run beneath
.IR codeforces/contest/index/ ,
commands infer the problem automatically.
.B submit
may also use the most recently opened problem.
A numeric contest argument is the ID in
.IR /contest/id/ ,
not the displayed round number.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I codeforces/contest/index/solution.cpp
User solution.
.TP
.I .cfx/solution.cpp
Optional archive-owned starter template. It takes precedence over the packaged
template.
.TP
.I codeforces/contest/index/cases/
Handwritten and promoted regression cases.
.TP
.I codeforces/contest/index/stress/gen.cpp
Default stress generator.
.TP
.I codeforces/contest/index/stress/brute.cpp
Default brute-force implementation.
.TP
.I codeforces/contest/index/problem.json
Fetched problem metadata and resource limits.
.TP
.I include/cp/
Extensionless, submission-safe headers providing contracts, debugging,
disjoint sets, Fenwick and segment trees, modular integers,
Knuth-Morris-Pratt matching,
.BR chmin ,
and
.BR chmax .
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/cfx/workspaces/
Fetched samples, build cache, stress failures, current-problem state, and
prepared submission artifacts. When
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
is unset, cfx uses
.IR $HOME/.local/state/cfx/workspaces/ .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CXX
C++ compiler command.
The default is
.BR c++ .
.TP
.B CFX_STD
C++ language standard.
The default is
.BR c++20 .
.TP
.B CFX_CXXFLAGS
Additional compiler flags.
.TP
.B CFX_ROOT
Explicit solution archive root.
.TP
.B CFX_STATE_ROOT
Explicit runtime-state root, primarily for isolated environments and tests.
.TP
.B EDITOR
Editor used when opening
.IR solution.cpp .
.TP
.B VISUAL
Editor fallback when
.B EDITOR
is unset.
.TP
.B CFX_BROWSER
Browser-opening command override.
.TP
.B CFX_CLIPBOARD
Clipboard command override.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The operation succeeded.
For
.BR submit ,
the verdict was
.B OK
on
.BR TESTS .
For
.BR "test \-\-remote-check" ,
all inputs completed within their limits; output correctness remains unchecked.
.TP
.B 1
Tests or stress checking failed, or submit reported a final non-Accepted
verdict.
.TP
.B 2
Usage was invalid, an operational error occurred, or submission remains
pending or requires manual completion.
.SH EXAMPLES
Fetch and solve a problem:
.PP
.nf
cfx 71A
cfx submit
.fi
.PP
For a problem with multiple valid outputs:
.PP
.nf
cfx test --remote-check 2250B
cfx submit --remote-check 2250B
.fi
.PP
Run sanitizer-backed tests:
.PP
.nf
cfx test --checked
.fi
.PP
Differential-test 10,000 deterministic inputs and preserve a mismatch:
.PP
.nf
cfx stress -n 10000 --seed 1
cfx fail
cfx test
.fi
.PP
Produce a standalone submission:
.PP
.nf
cfx bundle -o submission.cpp
.fi
.PP
Import one Competitive Companion problem:
.PP
.nf
cfx cc --once
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR c++ (1),
.BR git (1)
